# Dependency pins - the pin record.
#
# Format: <name> <upstream-commit-or-tag> <license-id> <upstream-url>
#
# Despia MCP vendors NO source tree. What it pins are the two official Model
# Context Protocol SDKs, consumed as ordinary package-manager dependencies
# (SPM on the Swift lane, Maven on the Kotlin lane). They are recorded here for
# the same three reasons the other packages record vendored trees:
#
#   1. PERMISSIVE ONLY. Both SDKs are MIT. ai_package_gate.rb checks the licence
#      id in this file against the schema's copyleft dimension, so a future bump
#      to a copyleft dependency fails a gate instead of a review.
#   2. PINNED, NEVER FLOATING. MCP has already churned its transports and its
#      auth story once. An exact version is the only defensible pin for a
#      protocol that moves: bumps go through a PR that runs the full gate set,
#      and the negotiated wire version is asserted by the conformance corpus.
#   3. ONE SOURCE OF TRUTH. Package.swift and bindings/kotlin*/build.gradle.kts
#      carry the same two versions; this file is what a reviewer reads first.
#
# The wire protocol version these pins negotiate is 2025-11-25 (the SDKs' own
# latest supported revision); older revisions remain accepted on the client.

